644:
It is the purpose of this article to protect the health, safety, and welfare of the citizens of the City by providing basic licensing requirements for peddlers and solicitors operating in the City. With this article, the City Council seeks to balance the First Amendment rights of peddlers and solicitors with the governmental interest and responsibility to protect life and property. The First Amendment affords Persons the right to travel along public streets and thoroughfares, enabling Solicitors and Peddlers to cold call on residents, which generates a significant amount of complaints to the City annually. Complaints have included claims that solicitors were aggressive, relentless, and on occasion, would not immediately leave the premises when asked to do so. Additionally, the City Council sets forth the following objectives with this article:
(1) To provide reasonable and expedient licensing requirements for door-to-door solicitors and peddlers;
(2) To protect the safety of the public by verifying the identity and backgrounds of solicitors and peddlers;
(3) To protect residents, peddlers, and solicitors by requesting door-to-door activity and location routes;
(4) To protect private property rights;
(5) To provide for penalties for violations of this article;
(6) To provide for due process; and
(7) To efficiently allocate City resources.
(Code 2005, § 66-29; Ord. No. 7390-2021, exh. A(66-29), 9-13-2021)

