(a) Additional information. Application for a license under this article shall be made as provided in Article III of this chapter, except that such application shall contain the additional information listed below. Application shall be submitted to Development Services and will be routed to the Police Chief or his or her designee for review.
(1) Name and address of present place of residence and length of residence at such address; also business address if other than present address;
(2) Address of place of residence during the past three years if other than present address;
(3) Age of applicant;
(4) Name and address of the person firm or corporation or association whom the applicant is employed by or represents and the length of time of such employment or representation;
(5) Name and address of employer during the past three years if other than the present employer;
(6) Description sufficient for identification of the subject matter of the soliciting in which the applicant will engage;
(7) Period of time for which the license is applied;
(8) Proposed route, including streets to be included on each day, which applicant intends to follow if soliciting from house to house or road to road. The first day shall begin on the first day the permit is valid and proceed through the last day the permit is valid;
(9) The date, or approximate date, of the latest previous application for license under this chapter, if any;
(10) Whether the applicant has ever been convicted of a felony, a crime of moral turpitude, or any other violation of any State or federal law;
(11) Proposed method of operation;
(12) Description and license plate number of vehicles intended to be operated by the applicant for the purpose of engaging in soliciting, if any;
(13) Signature of applicant;
(14) Social security number of applicant, for the purposes of reviewing the criminal history of the applicant, unless a criminal history is provided as described under Subsection (a)(15) of this section;
(15) Background check. In lieu of providing a social security number to Development Services, an applicant can also submit a criminal history completed with another law enforcement agency in the State within the last 90 days, along with an affidavit from the applicant attesting to its authenticity.
(b) Sworn statements. All statements made by the applicant upon the application or in connection therewith shall be under oath.
(c) Criminal history review. No license shall be issued to any person who has been convicted of a felony or crime of moral turpitude within five years of the date of the application; nor to any person who has been convicted of a violation of any of the provisions of this chapter; nor to any person whose license issued hereunder has previously been revoked as herein provided nor to any person who has been found to have made fraudulent statements on the application.
(d) Review and decision. Once submitted, the license application review shall be completed within 30 calendar days from the submittal date. The applicant shall be notified of approval or denial of the application no later than 30 calendar days from the receipt of the completed application, which includes the payment of the required fees. The reasons for denial shall be stated in writing and mailed by certified mail, return receipt requested or personally served to the applicant. If the application is not approved or denied within 30 days from the submittal date, it shall be deemed approved.
(e) Term/renewals. Each license issued under this article shall expire 90 days from the date of issuance, but may be renewed prior to expiration for up to three additional 90 day terms with the successful completion of a background check as outlined in this article. Once the license expires, a person must apply for a new license.
(Code 1989, § 9-3-3; Code 2005, § 66-33; Ord. No. 005-2007, 3-12-2007; Ord. No. 7390-2021, exh. A(66-33), 9-13-2021)

